-- title:
--   Transport of chart poles to the level field, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime equal to $3$ (the hypothesis `hq3`), $M'$ is a nonzero natural number, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$. Write $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Recall the project's fields of Laurent series: `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` is the subfield of $\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j(\mathsf q^d)$ for $d \mid M'$; `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of that field; `fieldBar q M'` is the analogous base change of the $\Gamma_H$-function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; and `modularFunctionFieldC K N` is $K(j, j(\mathsf q^N))$.
--
--   The data are: a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; a finite set $W$ of places (in the project's sense: a proper valuation subring containing the constants, with principal ideal ring of integers) of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, together with a distinguished $s \in W$; an inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into `fieldBar q M'`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` whose constants are $A$, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with orders); an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with elements $\pi_0, \zeta_0, \varpi_t, \xi$ and $\pi_0 \in A$; a natural number $\ell$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$ (hypothesis `hAb`) and an element $\varpi_b \in A_b$; a subgroup $H_1 \leq (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0((\mathsf q))/k_0$, an $A_0$-algebra structure on $K_\ell$ in a scalar tower with $k_0$, where $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ denotes `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ Q̄)`; a nonzero $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ and an element $\varpi_t' \in A_0$; an ideal $y$ of $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ`, the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; a subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ over $A_0$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`); natural numbers $n, m$, a matrix $\gamma_0 \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, an automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, an element $a_0 \in A_0$, a proof `hjK` that $j(\mathsf q^q) =$ `jqNModC k₀ q` lies in $K_\ell$, and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$.
--
--   The hypotheses fall into the following groups, all of which are assumed. Arithmetic of the level: `hqM'` ($q \nmid M'$), `hA` ($A$ lies over $q$, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$), `hH₁` ($H_1$ is the intersection of `levelH q M'` with the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$, so the units congruent to $1$ both modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$), `htame` ($\ell_g - 1$ is a unit of $A_0$), `hξ` ($\xi$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity), and the auxiliary-prime group `hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`, `hζ₀` ($\ell$ is prime, $\ell \geq 3$, $\ell \neq q$, $\ell \nmid M'$, and $\zeta_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity), together with `hϖtA`, `hϖt` ($\varpi_t \in A$ and $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$), `hKb`, `hϖb`, `hϖb0` ($K_b$ is the bottom field, the maximal ideal of $A_b$ is generated by the nonzero $\varpi_b$), and `hϖt'` ($\varpi_t' = \varpi_t$). Supersingular places: `hW` says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the set of places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and with $w$-value of the generator $j$ a supersingular $j$-invariant (every elliptic curve with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point). Compatibility of $R_0$ with coefficientwise reduction: `hR₀`. Local algebra of the base: `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ` ($A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and every element of $A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$). Identification of the upstairs field: `hKℓ` ($K_\ell$ is the base change to $k_0$ of `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁`) and `hjℓ` ($j_\ell$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$). The chosen chart point: `hy` ($y$ maximal), `hϖy` ($\pi_0 \in y$), `hss` (for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring map $C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the image of $j_\ell$ is a supersingular $j$-invariant), `hjC` and `ha₀y` ($j(\mathsf q^q) \in C$ and $j(\mathsf q^q) - a_0 \in y$). Matching of $y$ with the place $s$, and orbit transitivity: `hover` states that for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which $j$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue equals the value of the $R_0$-residue of $g$ at $s$, the element $g - c$ of $C$ lies in $y$; `hOrbit` states that every maximal ideal $y'$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ satisfying this same matching condition is carried to $y$ by some level automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $C$. Here a level automorphism at $\gamma$ is `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ Kℓ τ`: $\tau$ multiplies $q$-expansions of ratios of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$-modular forms in the way prescribed by the action of $\gamma$ conjugated by $\mathrm{diag}(1,1/q)$, under any embedding sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$.
--
--   The rigid chart hypothesis `hS1` (thirteen clauses, summarised here) requires: $C \subseteq B_t$; $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$; $B_t/(\pi_0)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; the constants of $W_t$ are $A_0$, its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, it is a discrete valuation ring, $y$ is the contraction of $\mathfrak m_{W_t}$ to $C$, and $W_t$ is the localisation of $B_t$ at $\mathfrak m_{W_t}$; for each algebra structure of $\mathbb F_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2` on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements lying in $\mathfrak m_{W_t}$, compatible with constants, and equivariant for level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ via an element $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma, c)$ of the Drinfeld subgroup [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$, and with the same scalar $c$ realised together with the identity matrix by some further $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau'$; $B_t$ is stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ receives the $\mathfrak m_{W_t}$-part of $B_t$ under some such $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; and any $b \in B_t$ all of whose translates lie in $\mathfrak m_{W_t}$ is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   The deck-group and crossing data consist of: `hn1`, `hnq` ($1 \leq n$ and $n \mid q+1$), `hn` ($n = 2\,$`placeWidthChar q M' s`, the width $6$ or $1$ at $q=3$ according as the $j$-value at $s$ vanishes or not, divided by the ramification of $j$ at $s$), `hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`, `hτ₀`, `hτ₀W` ($\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W_t$), `hm1`, `hm` ($1 \leq m$ and $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t'$ times a unit), `hζc`, `hζcprim` ($\zeta_c^n = 1$ and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ is a unit for $0 < k < n$), and the hypothesis `hR7` (twelve top-level clauses, summarised here): $\tau_0$ has exact order $n$ on $B_t$ and every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power of $\tau_0$; `ends` has $q+1$ elements, is permuted by the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$, transitively so, is stabilised elementwise by $\tau_0$, and distinct ends are separated by an element that is a unit in one and not in the other; there is a finite-type, $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-stable subalgebra $B_c$ contained in every end, of which each end is a localisation; an end mapped into $W_t$ by $\tau$ forces $\tau$ to preserve $W_t$; and each end $O$ is contained in $W_t$, is local and noetherian, contains $C$, has constants $A_0$, has every element congruent to a constant, and its adic completion is identified with the crossing model $\mathbb W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^m)$ over the completion of $A_0$ in such a way that constants are constants, two elements $c_x, c_y$ of $O$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m u$ correspond to unit multiples of $U$ and of $V$ (with $c_y \in \mathfrak m_{W_t}$, $c_x \notin \mathfrak m_{W_t}$), $j(\mathsf q^q) - a_0$ corresponds to a unit times $V^e$ with $e \geq 1$, and $\tau_0$ corresponds to an automorphism $\theta_0$ scaling $U$ by $\zeta_c$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c^{-1}$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; for each end there is moreover a discrete valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ (containing $O$ and $C$, with constants $A_0$ and uniformiser $\pi_0$, residually transcendental at a parameter and at $j(\mathsf q^q)$, with $c_x \in \mathfrak m_{W_x}$, $c_y \notin \mathfrak m_{W_x}$, cutting out $y$ on $C$ but not dominating it, escaped by the other ends and characterising $O$ among the ends) and a finite-type, stable subalgebra $B_x \subseteq B_t \cap O$ of which $O$ is a localisation, whose elements have no poles where $j_\ell$ has none, and containing an element escaping every valuation subring of $j$-Igusa type that some element of $O$ escapes; finally a dichotomy: any valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$, containing $C$ and dominating $y$, either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends. Two further escape hypotheses are assumed: `hR9`, the existence of $b \in B_t$ outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal and $j_\ell$ residually transcendental (no monic polynomial over $A_0$ evaluated at $j_\ell$ falls into the maximal ideal); and `hR10`, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ that is not in the level-automorphism orbit of $y$, the existence of $b \in B_t$ outside every valuation subring dominating a translate of $y''$.
--
--   Finally the descent naming block: $G$ is the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`), $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`), $B_0$ consists of the elements of $B_t$ fixed by $G$ (`hB₀`), and $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ whose elements are those lying in $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   The conclusion, stated with $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, is the following. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ such that (CHAR) an element $f$ lies in $F_0$ precisely when every Laurent coefficient of $f$, for each $n \in \mathbb Z$, lies in the image of $k_0$; let $\varphi : K_0 \to F_0$ be an isomorphism of $k_0$-algebras such that (φ1) the coefficientwise extension of scalars along $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ takes the Laurent series of $f \in K_0$ to the Laurent series of $\varphi f$; (φ4) for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$), every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi' \in k_0$ with $\zeta = \xi'$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ at $\gamma$ relative to $(q,\xi',q,q^2M',H_1)$: $\tau$ maps $K_0$ into $K_0$, and $\varphi(\tau f) =$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $(\varphi f)$ for all $f \in K_0$; (φ5) for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose coefficientwise image in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in $K_0$, $\varphi$ of that element is the image under `hle` of the base change of $g$ to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $F_0$ obtained by transporting $W_0'$ along $\varphi$ (formally, the preimage of $W_0'$ under $\varphi^{-1}$); $W_0$ is quantified over but does not occur in the assertion that follows. Let $B$ be the subring of `fieldBar q M'` consisting exactly of the images, under $\varphi$ followed by the inclusion $F_0 \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, of the elements of $K_0$ that lie in $B_0$.
--
--   Assume the two upstairs escape statements. (hE1′): there is $b \in K_0$ with $b \in B_0$ such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with constants $A$, i.e. $x \in A \iff x \in V$ for $x \in k_0$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, and such that the image of `coeffEmb k₀ jq` lies in $K_0$ and in $V$ and is residually transcendental there: for every monic $p \in k_0[X]$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, the value $p(j)$ is not in the maximal ideal of $V$. (hE3′): for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \neq s$ there is $b \in K_0$ with $b \in B_0$ such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with constants $A$ as above and with the property that, for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers`, which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which $j$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s'$, the element `coeffEmb k₀ g` (whenever it lies in $K_\ell$) lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals the value at $s'$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   Then both of the following hold. First, there is $b \in$ `fieldBar q M'` lying in $F_0$ and in $B$ such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ whose constants are $A$ (for $x \in k_0$: $x \in A \iff x \in V$), with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, and such that the image under `hle` in `fieldBar q M'` of the base change of `jq` to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $F_0$, lies in $V$, and is residually transcendental there in the same sense (no monic polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ takes it into the maximal ideal of $V$). Second, for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \neq s$ there is $b \in$ `fieldBar q M'` lying in $F_0$ and in $B$ such that $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ whose constants are $A$ and such that, for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, is regular wherever $j$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s'$, the image under `hle` of that base change lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue equals the value at $s'$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference lies in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   This is the descent step of the supersingular-chart analysis in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ diamond frame at $q = 3$: it carries the two separation ("pole") statements — one against valuations of $j$-Igusa type, one against the supersingular places of $W$ other than $s$ — from the fixed field $K_0$ of the level-automorphism group $G$ inside $K_\ell$ down to the level field $F_0$ inside `fieldBar q M'`, along the isomorphism $\varphi$ and with $B_0$ replaced by its image $B$. It feeds the constructor [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd), which assembles the semistable model data at the supersingular points.
